Carafe: the settings menu is drawn over the game's frame with the frame showing through.
When wine_nx_osk_translucent (runtime/overlay/carafe_menu.c) says the layer is half-transparent, the menu's
picture goes into a texture once per change and a render pass blends it over the image about to be shown, so
the frame never leaves the GPU. Swapchain images get COLOR_ATTACHMENT for that when the surface allows it.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

